      "nodes": [
        {
          "t": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "What Is Orthokeratology?",
          "html": "What Is Orthokeratology?",
          "align": "center",
          "id": "srYAZIswqC",
          "col": 0,
          "origin": "static"
        },
        {
          "t": "html",
          "html": "<p>Orthokeratology, often called ortho-k, uses custom-fit contact lenses that you wear while you sleep. As you rest, the lenses gently reshape the front surface of your eyes. By morning, you can remove them and see clearly throughout the day—no glasses or daytime contacts needed. The effect is temporary, making it a safe and flexible option for many patients.</p>",
          "align": "center",
          "id": "VKYJYx3trs",
          "col": 0,
          "origin": "static"
        },
        {
